  {
    icon: "🔐",
    title: "Hardware-backed identities",
    body: "Your private key is generated inside hardware and cannot be read, copied, or exfiltrated: the Secure Enclave of an Apple Silicon Mac (Touch ID), or a YubiKey PIV slot (PIN and a touch) on Intel Macs and Linux. Only the public recipient is ever shared.",
    span: "feature--xl",
    tag: "hardware",
  },
  {
    icon: "📦",
    title: "One-command bootstrap",
    body: "<code>sopsy init</code> installs missing tools, then writes .sops.yaml, .env.example, an encrypted .env.encrypted, .gitignore safety rules, and .sopsy.yml, and sets up the break-glass key. Idempotent — re-running is always safe.",
    span: "feature--md",
    tag: "init",
  },
  {
    icon: "🗝️",
